GFG — Children Sum in a Binary Tree
Problem Understanding

The Children Sum Property says:

For every non-leaf node, its value must equal the sum of its existing children.

So:

Two children
node.data = node.left.data + node.right.data
Only left child
node.data = node.left.data
Only right child
node.data = node.right.data
Leaf node

A leaf has no children, so there is nothing to check.

Example 1 — Valid Tree
            10
           /  \
          8    2
         / \    \
        5   3    2

Check:

10 = 8 + 2   ✓
 8 = 5 + 3   ✓
 2 = 2       ✓

So:

true
Example 2 — Invalid Tree
            10
           /  \
          8    3
         / \
        5   3

At root:

10 != 8 + 3

Therefore:

false
Important Observation

Unlike many tree problems, this is a local property.

For each node, we only need:

current node
    +
its immediate children

We don't need:

subtree sums
ancestors
horizontal distance
paths
global information

So every solution fundamentally needs to visit each node once.

That means there isn't a natural O(n²) brute force solution that is useful here. The "brute force" version is simply a straightforward two-pass validation, while the optimal versions validate during the traversal itself.

Approach 1 — Brute Force: Collect All Nodes, Then Validate
Idea

First traverse the whole tree and store every node.

Then in a second pass:

for every node:
    if leaf → skip
    calculate child sum
    compare with node.data

It's straightforward, but we store all nodes unnecessarily.

Code
import java.util.*;

class Solution {

    void collectNodes(Node root, List<Node> nodes) {

        if (root == null) {
            return;
        }

        nodes.add(root);

        collectNodes(root.left, nodes);
        collectNodes(root.right, nodes);
    }

    public boolean isSumProperty(Node root) {

        if (root == null) {
            return true;
        }

        List<Node> nodes = new ArrayList<>();

        // First traversal
        collectNodes(root, nodes);

        // Second traversal through stored nodes
        for (Node curr : nodes) {

            // Leaf node
            if (curr.left == null && curr.right == null) {
                continue;
            }

            int sum = 0;

            if (curr.left != null) {
                sum += curr.left.data;
            }

            if (curr.right != null) {
                sum += curr.right.data;
            }

            if (curr.data != sum) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
}

