Why size = q.size() Is Not Actually Necessary Here

You use:

int size = q.size();
for(int i = 0; i < size; i++)

But unlike:

Level Order Traversal
Zigzag Traversal
Right Side View

we don't need to distinguish levels.

The Children Sum Property is checked independently for every node.

Therefore this is enough:

while (!q.isEmpty()) {

    Node curr = q.poll();

    // check curr

    if (curr.left != null) q.add(curr.left);
    if (curr.right != null) q.add(curr.right);
}

So we can make the BFS even simpler.

