Where:

n = number of nodes
h = tree height
w = maximum width
Which Is Most Optimal?

There is an important point here:

Time

All sensible approaches are:

O(n)

because every node may need to be checked.

Auxiliary space

Recursive DFS uses:

O(h)

which is generally the smallest standard auxiliary-space bound.

So I would call:

Recursive DFS

the best standard solution.

Your BFS solution is also time-optimal, but its queue can require O(w) space.

